cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RaGCAn, please cite it as below."
title: "RaGCAn: Rapid Genome Coherence Analyzer"
abstract: >
  A rapid core-genome screen that asks whether a named prokaryotic genus holds
  together. RaGCAn builds the core proteome of a set of genomes, computes
  average amino-acid identity between every pair, and partitions the set by
  complete-linkage clustering. A genus that returns one bin is coherent. More
  than one bin is a proposed re-categorisation.
type: software
version: 3.0.0
license: MIT
